\title{ReproducibleCDI: Reproducing the Community Deprivation Index of Neighborhood Socioeconomic Status}
\description{
Provides a simple, tidy interface for calculating the Community Deprivation Index (CDI), a composite measure of neighborhood-level socioeconomic deprivation, using data from the US Census Bureau's American Community Survey (ACS). The CDI follows the Singh/Area Deprivation Index (ADI) methodology - a principal-component-weighted composite of 18 standardized ACS variables - and adds a percentage-uninsured variable. The variables match the official CMS reference implementation exactly. computeOriginalCDI() reproduces every CMS step at the block-group level (margin-of-error-based empirical Bayes stabilization toward the tract, hierarchical block group -> tract -> county -> state imputation, group-quarters / low-population suppression, and SAS-style 1-100 ranks). computeCDI() builds the index the way the sibling ReproducibleX packages do, at county, tract, or block-group level, with optional stabilization and spatial imputation in a user-chosen order.
}
